, printf(%s) will dereference it as a string — potential crash or info leak.\"}],\"facts\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Binary is ELF64 x86-64 PIE, dynamically linked, not stripped, compiled with GCC 10.2.0\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F002\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Security: Full RELRO, NX enabled, Canary found, PIE enabled, no FORTIFY\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F003\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"libc is Ubuntu GLIBC 2.39-0ubuntu8.8 at /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6\",\"source\":\"RUNTIME\"},{\"id\":\"F004\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"BSS layout: msg[32] at 0x4060 (256 bytes, 8-byte pointers), msg_size[32] at 0x4160 (128 bytes, 4-byte ints), urandom FILE* at 0x41e0, cookie_num at 0x41e8\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F005\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"init() opens /dev/urandom, stores FILE* in urandom(0x41e0), creates 5 initial cookies via strdup with sizes 80,48,24,56,64, sets cookie_num=5\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F006\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie reads index via scanf(%llu) as unsigned long long, but checks with 'cmp rdx,rax; jl' (signed less-than) at 0x1681-0x1684\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F007\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie reads index via scanf(%llu) as unsigned long long, but checks with 'cmp rdx,rax; jl' (signed less-than) at 0x17aa-0x17ad\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F008\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie writes to msg[index] via read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1) — index used in lea rdx,[rax*8] for pointer array addressing\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F009\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie prints msg[index] via printf(%s, msg[index]) — dereferences msg[index] as string pointer\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F010\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie: rand_idx = (signed char)fread_byte % cookie_num via idiv (signed division). free(msg[rand_idx]), then msg[rand_idx]=msg[cookie_num-1], msg_size[rand_idx]=msg_size[cookie_num-1], cookie_num--\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F011\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie does NOT clear msg[cookie_num-1] after moving it to msg[rand_idx] — the pointer remains in the old slot\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F012\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"create_cookie reads length via scanf(%lld) signed, checks length <= 0x100 with jle (signed), then calloc(length,1) and read(0,buf,length)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F013\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"GOT is read-only (Full RELRO): free@0x3f70, puts@0x3f78, fread@0x3f80, read@0x3fa0, printf@0x3f90, setvbuf@0x3fb0, fopen@0x3fb8, exit@0x3fc8\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F014\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"alarm(60) called in init — process will receive SIGALRM after 60 seconds\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F015\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg array (0x4060) has 32 entries spanning 0x4060-0x415f. msg_size (0x4160) has 32 entries spanning 0x4160-0x41df. urandom at 0x41e0 is 0x180 bytes offset from msg[0]. msg_size[31] at 0x41dc is the last 4-byte entry before urandom.\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F016\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"An OOB index of -8 (0xfffffffffffffff8 signed) in edit_cookie/read_cookie would address msg[-8] = 0x4060 - 0x40 = 0x4020 = stdout. Index -7 = stdin(0x4030), -4 = 0x4040=stderr. Positive OOB: index 32 = 0x4160 = msg_size[0], index 64 = 0x41e0 = urandom, index 65 = 0x41e8 = cookie_num.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F017\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"Since index is %llu (unsigned) but checked with jl (signed), any value with bit 63 set (>= 0x8000000000000000) is interpreted as negative by jl and passes the check if < cookie_num (signed). This includes values like 0xfffffffffffffff8 (-8 signed).\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F018\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"_abort function at 0x11f5 prints error message via printf then calls exit(1) — does not use abort() or __stack_chk_fail\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"CET (IBT/SHSTK) status cannot be determined from available tools\",\"reason\":\"checksec did not report CET flags, need readelf -n for GNU_PROPERTY note\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"ASLR status at runtime not confirmed\",\"reason\":\"Requires runtime observation of address randomization\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"Exact behavior of calloc with negative size argument\",\"reason\":\"Depends on libc implementation — may return NULL or wrap to large allocation\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"Whether msg[cookie_num-1] old pointer after eat_cookie move is accessible\",\"reason\":\"cookie_num is decremented, so the slot is technically out of active range, but OOB index in edit/read_cookie could reach it\"},{\"id\":\"U005\",\"description\":\"Whether signed idiv in eat_cookie can produce negative rand_idx\",\"reason\":\"fread reads 1 byte into int, cdqe sign-extends to 64-bit, idiv with cookie_num — if byte has MSB set, result is negative. Need to verify if negative index is used for msg[] access.\"},{\"id\":\"U006\",\"description\":\"seccomp/sandbox status unknown\",\"reason\":\"No seccomp filter detected in static analysis, but runtime sandbox not confirmed\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF64 LSB PIE, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, not stripped, GCC 10.2.0. Entry=0x1110. Segments: LOAD R(0x0-0x900), LOAD RX(0x1000-0x19ad), LOAD R(0x2000-0x24c0), LOAD RW(0x3d58-0x41f0). GNU_STACK RW (no exec).\",\"sections\":\".text 0x1110 sz=0x891 RX | .rodata 0x2000 sz=0x266 R | .data 0x4000 sz=0x10 RW | .bss 0x4020 sz=0x1d0 RW | .got 0x3f58 sz=0xa8 R(FullRELRO) | .plt 0x1020 sz=0xe0 RX | .init_array 0x3d58 sz=8 RW | .fini_array 0x3d60 sz=8 RW | .dynamic 0x3d68 sz=0x1f0 RW\",\"symbols\":\"msg 0x4060 OBJECT 256 | msg_size 0x4160 OBJECT 128 | urand