, printf(%s) will dereference it as a string — potential crash or info leak.\"}],\"facts\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Binary is ELF64 x86-64 PIE, dynamically linked, not stripped, compiled with GCC 10.2.0\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F002\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Security: Full RELRO, NX enabled, Canary found, PIE enabled, no FORTIFY\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F003\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"libc is Ubuntu GLIBC 2.39-0ubuntu8.8 at /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6\",\"source\":\"RUNTIME\"},{\"id\":\"F004\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"BSS layout: msg[32] at 0x4060 (256 bytes, 8-byte pointers), msg_size[32] at 0x4160 (128 bytes, 4-byte ints), urandom FILE* at 0x41e0, cookie_num at 0x41e8\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F005\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"init() opens /dev/urandom, stores FILE* in urandom(0x41e0), creates 5 initial cookies via strdup with sizes 80,48,24,56,64, sets cookie_num=5\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F006\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie reads index via scanf(%llu) as unsigned long long, but checks with 'cmp rdx,rax; jl' (signed less-than) at 0x1681-0x1684\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F007\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie reads index via scanf(%llu) as unsigned long long, but checks with 'cmp rdx,rax; jl' (signed less-than) at 0x17aa-0x17ad\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F008\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie writes to msg[index] via read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1) — index used in lea rdx,[rax*8] for pointer array addressing\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F009\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie prints msg[index] via printf(%s, msg[index]) — dereferences msg[index] as string pointer\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F010\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie: rand_idx = (signed char)fread_byte % cookie_num via idiv (signed division). free(msg[rand_idx]), then msg[rand_idx]=msg[cookie_num-1], msg_size[rand_idx]=msg_size[cookie_num-1], cookie_num--\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F011\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie does NOT clear msg[cookie_num-1] after moving it to msg[rand_idx] — the pointer remains in the old slot\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F012\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"create_cookie reads length via scanf(%lld) signed, checks length <= 0x100 with jle (signed), then calloc(length,1) and read(0,buf,length)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F013\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"GOT is read-only (Full RELRO): free@0x3f70, puts@0x3f78, fread@0x3f80, read@0x3fa0, printf@0x3f90, setvbuf@0x3fb0, fopen@0x3fb8, exit@0x3fc8\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F014\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"alarm(60) called in init — process will receive SIGALRM after 60 seconds\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F015\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg array (0x4060) has 32 entries spanning 0x4060-0x415f. msg_size (0x4160) has 32 entries spanning 0x4160-0x41df. urandom at 0x41e0 is 0x180 bytes offset from msg[0]. msg_size[31] at 0x41dc is the last 4-byte entry before urandom.\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F016\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"An OOB index of -8 (0xfffffffffffffff8 signed) in edit_cookie/read_cookie would address msg[-8] = 0x4060 - 0x40 = 0x4020 = stdout. Index -7 = stdin(0x4030), -4 = 0x4040=stderr. Positive OOB: index 32 = 0x4160 = msg_size[0], index 64 = 0x41e0 = urandom, index 65 = 0x41e8 = cookie_num.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F017\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"Since index is %llu (unsigned) but checked with jl (signed), any value with bit 63 set (>= 0x8000000000000000) is interpreted as negative by jl and passes the check if < cookie_num (signed). This includes values like 0xfffffffffffffff8 (-8 signed).\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F018\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"_abort function at 0x11f5 prints error message via printf then calls exit(1) — does not use abort() or __stack_chk_fail\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"CET (IBT/SHSTK) status cannot be determined from available tools\",\"reason\":\"checksec did not report CET flags, need readelf -n for GNU_PROPERTY note\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"ASLR status at runtime not confirmed\",\"reason\":\"Requires runtime observation of address randomization\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"Exact behavior of calloc with negative size argument\",\"reason\":\"Depends on libc implementation — may return NULL or wrap to large allocation\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"Whether msg[cookie_num-1] old pointer after eat_cookie move is accessible\",\"reason\":\"cookie_num is decremented, so the slot is technically out of active range, but OOB index in edit/read_cookie could reach it\"},{\"id\":\"U005\",\"description\":\"Whether signed idiv in eat_cookie can produce negative rand_idx\",\"reason\":\"fread reads 1 byte into int, cdqe sign-extends to 64-bit, idiv with cookie_num — if byte has MSB set, result is negative. Need to verify if negative index is used for msg[] access.\"},{\"id\":\"U006\",\"description\":\"seccomp/sandbox status unknown\",\"reason\":\"No seccomp filter detected in static analysis, but runtime sandbox not confirmed\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF64 LSB PIE, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, not stripped, GCC 10.2.0. Entry=0x1110. Segments: LOAD R(0x0-0x900), LOAD RX(0x1000-0x19ad), LOAD R(0x2000-0x24c0), LOAD RW(0x3d58-0x41f0). GNU_STACK RW (no exec).\",\"sections\":\".text 0x1110 sz=0x891 RX | .rodata 0x2000 sz=0x266 R | .data 0x4000 sz=0x10 RW | .bss 0x4020 sz=0x1d0 RW | .got 0x3f58 sz=0xa8 R(FullRELRO) | .plt 0x1020 sz=0xe0 RX | .init_array 0x3d58 sz=8 RW | .fini_array 0x3d60 sz=8 RW | .dynamic 0x3d68 sz=0x1f0 RW\",\"symbols\":\"msg 0x4060 OBJECT 256 | msg_size 0x4160 OBJECT 128 | urandom 0x41e0 OBJECT 8 | cookie_num 0x41e8 OBJECT 8 | stdout 0x4020 | stdin 0x4030 | stderr 0x4040 | main 0x187f | init 0x1232 | create_cookie 0x1399 | eat_cookie 0x14e1 | edit_cookie 0x1628 | read_cookie 0x1751 | menu 0x17fd | _abort 0x11f5\",\"disassembly\":\"edit_cookie 0x1628: scanf(%llu)->rbp-0x10; cmp rdx,[cookie_num]; jl 0x1692; read(0, msg[idx], msg_size[idx]-1). read_cookie 0x1751: scanf(%llu)->rbp-0x10; cmp rdx,[cookie_num]; jl 0x17bb; printf(%s, msg[idx]). eat_cookie 0x14e1: fread 1 byte from urandom; idiv cookie_num; free(msg[rand]); msg[rand]=msg[cookie_num-1]; cookie_num--. create_cookie 0x1399: scanf(%lld)->len; cmp len,0x100; jle; calloc(len,1); read(0,buf,len); msg[cookie_num]=buf; msg_size[cookie_num]=len; cookie_num++.\"}},\"vulnerability_report\":{\"schema\":\"VulnerabilityReport\",\"version\":\"1.0\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"summary\":{\"total_bugs\":5,\"high_severity\":3,\"medium_severity\":2,\"low_severity\":0},\"vulnerabilities\":[{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"title\":\"INDEX_SIGNEDNESS_MISMATCH_IN_EDIT_AND_READ_COOKIE\",\"root_cause\":{\"type\":\"Signedness Error\",\"description\":\"In edit_cookie and read_cookie, the cookie index is read via scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") as unsigned long long, but the bounds check uses 'jl' (signed less-than) to compare index against cookie_num. Any value with bit 63 set (>= 0x8000000000000000) is interpreted as negative by the signed jl comparison and passes the check (since a large negative is < cookie_num). The index is then used as an unsigned multiplier in 'lea rdx,[rax*8]' to address the msg[] array at 0x4060, producing an out-of-bounds access to arbitrary BSS locations relative to msg[].\"},\"affected_functions\":[\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\"],\"affected_objects\":[\"msg[32] at 0x4060\",\"msg_size[32] at 0x4160\",\"urandom FILE* at 0x41e0\",\"cookie_num at 0x41e8\",\"stdout at 0x4020\",\"stdin at 0x4030\",\"stderr at 0x4040\"],\"attack_surface\":{\"input\":\"cookie_index via scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") from stdin\",\"entry_function\":\"edit_cookie / read_cookie\",\"data_flow\":[\"stdin -> scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") -> rbp-0x10 (unsigned long long index)\",\"index loaded into rdx at 0x1676/0x179f\",\"cookie_num loaded into rax at 0x167a/0x17a3\",\"cmp rdx,rax; jl (signed comparison) at 0x1681-0x1684 / 0x17aa-0x17ad\",\"index used in lea rdx,[rax*8] for msg[] addressing at 0x16c3/0x17bf\",\"edit_cookie: read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1) — OOB write\",\"read_cookie: printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[index]) — OOB read + dereference\"]},\"security_check\":{\"expected\":\"Index should be validated as unsigned (0 <= index < cookie_num) using unsigned comparison (jb/jae)\",\"actual\":\"Index is compared with 'jl' (signed less-than), which treats values >= 0x8000000000000000 as negative and allows them to pass the check\",\"missing_or_incorrect\":\"Missing unsigned bounds check; signed comparison jl used instead of unsigned jb for an unsigned input\"},\"vulnerable_operation\":{\"operation\":\"OOB array access via lea rdx,[rax*8] + msg base\",\"address\":\"0x16c3 (edit_cookie), 0x17bf (read_cookie)\",\"expression\":\"msg[index] where index is attacker-controlled unsigned value that bypassed signed check\",\"target\":\"msg[] array at 0x4060 and adjacent BSS data (msg_size at 0x4160, urandom at 0x41e0, cookie_num at 0x41e8, stdout/stdin/stderr at 0x4020-0x4040)\",\"size\":\"8 bytes per pointer slot for msg[], 4 bytes per int slot for msg_size[]\"},\"impact\":[{\"type\":\"OOB_WRITE\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"In edit_cookie, the OOB index is used to compute msg[index] address and msg_size[index] value. read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1) writes attacker-controlled data to the OOB-retrieved pointer location. If the OOB slot contains a pointer to a sensitive BSS location (e.g., urandom FILE*, cookie_num), the write corrupts that data.\"},{\"type\":\"OOB_READ\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"In read_cookie, the OOB index retrieves a value from msg[] at an out-of-bounds offset. This value is passed to printf(\\\"%s\\\") as a string pointer and dereferenced, leaking memory contents at the address stored in the OOB slot. In edit_cookie, msg_size[index] is read OOB to determine the write length.\"},{\"type\":\"MEMORY_CORRUPTION\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"The OOB write in edit_cookie can corrupt BSS data structures including msg_size[], urandom FILE*, and cookie_num, leading to broader memory corruption.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E001\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1665-0x166c\",\"description\":\"scanf called with format string \\\"%llu\\\" (at 0x21c4 in .rodata), reading index as unsigned long long into rbp-0x10\"},{\"id\":\"E002\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1681-0x1684\",\"description\":\"cmp rdx,rax followed by jl 0x1692 — signed less-than comparison. rdx holds the unsigned index, rax holds cookie_num. A value like 0xfffffffffffffff8 (-8 signed) passes this check since -8 < 5 (signed).\"},{\"id\":\"E003\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16c3-0x16d2\",\"description\":\"lea rcx,[rax*8+0x0] then lea rax,[rip+0x298e] (# 4060 <msg>); mov rax,[rcx+rax*1] — index used as unsigned multiplier to address msg[] array. With index=0xfffffffffffffff8, computes 0x4060 + (-8*8) = 0x4060 - 0x40 = 0x4020 (stdout).\"},{\"id\":\"E004\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x178e-0x1795\",\"description\":\"scanf called with format string \\\"%llu\\\" (at 0x21c4), reading index as unsigned long long into rbp-0x10\"},{\"id\":\"E005\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17aa-0x17ad\",\"description\":\"cmp rdx,rax followed by jl 0x17bb — same signed less-than comparison as edit_cookie, same bypass\"},{\"id\":\"E006\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17bf-0x17ce\",\"description\":\"lea rdx,[rax*8+0x0] then lea rax,[rip+0x2892] (# 4060 <msg>); mov rax,[rdx+rax*1] — OOB index used to load pointer from msg[], then passed to printf as %s argument at 0x17e1\"},{\"id\":\"E007\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie/read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x4060\",\"description\":\"BSS layout analysis: msg[0] at 0x4060, msg[31] at 0x4158. Negative index -8 (0xfffffffffffffff8) addresses 0x4060-0x40=0x4020 (stdout). Positive OOB: index 32 addresses 0x4160 (msg_size[0]), index 64 addresses 0x41e0 (urandom), index 65 addresses 0x41e8 (cookie_num).\"}],\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"verification_required\":[\"Confirm that scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") with input like 18446744073709551608 (0xfffffffffffffff8) passes the jl check at runtime\",\"Verify the OOB write in edit_cookie can reach msg_size[], urandom, or cookie_num fields\",\"Verify the OOB read in read_cookie leaks memory via printf(\\\"%s\\\") dereferencing an OOB pointer value\"]},{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-002\",\"title\":\"SIGNED_DIVISION_NEGATIVE_INDEX_IN_EAT_COOKIE\",\"root_cause\":{\"type\":\"Signedness Error\",\"description\":\"In eat_cookie, a random byte from /dev/urandom is loaded as a 32-bit int, sign-extended to 64-bit via cdqe, then divided by cookie_num using idiv (signed division). If the random byte has its MSB set (>= 0x80), the sign-extended value is negative, and the signed division produces a negative remainder. This negative rand_idx is then sign-extended again via cdqe and used as an unsigned multiplier in 'lea rdx,[rax*8]' to index the msg[] array, producing an out-of-bounds access.\"},\"affected_functions\":[\"eat_cookie\"],\"affected_objects\":[\"msg[32] at 0x4060\",\"msg_size[32] at 0x4160\"],\"attack_surface\":{\"input\":\"random_byte from /dev/urandom (fread 1 byte)\",\"entry_function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"data_flow\":[\"/dev/urandom -> fread -> rbp-0xc (1 byte stored as int)\",\"mov eax,[rbp-0xc] at 0x1530 — loads byte as 32-bit int\",\"cdqe at 0x1533 — sign-extends to 64-bit (negative if MSB set)\",\"cqo at 0x153c — sign-extends for division\",\"idiv rcx at 0x153e — signed division by cookie_num, remainder in rdx\",\"rand_idx = remainder stored at rbp-0xc at 0x1544\",\"cdqe at 0x154a — sign-extends rand_idx again\",\"lea rdx,[rax*8] at 0x154c — used as unsigned offset to index msg[]\",\"printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[rand_idx]) at 0x156e — OOB read + dereference\",\"free(msg[rand_idx]) at 0x158e — OOB free\",\"msg[rand_idx] = msg[cookie_num-1] at 0x15c6 — OOB write\",\"msg_size[rand_idx] = msg_size[cookie_num-1] at 0x15fc — OOB write\"]},\"security_check\":{\"expected\":\"Random index should be computed as unsigned modulo: (unsigned char)byte % cookie_num, producing range [0, cookie_num-1]\",\"actual\":\"Byte is loaded as signed int, sign-extended, and divided with idiv (signed), producing a remainder in range [-(cookie_num-1), cookie_num-1]\",\"missing_or_incorrect\":\"Missing unsigned conversion of the random byte before division; signed idiv used instead of unsigned div\"},\"vulnerable_operation\":{\"operation\":\"OOB array access via lea rdx,[rax*8] + msg base, used for printf, free, and pointer assignment\",\"address\":\"0x154c-0x15c6\",\"expression\":\"msg[rand_idx] where rand_idx = (signed int)random_byte % cookie_num (signed idiv), can be negative\",\"target\":\"msg[] array at 0x4060 and adjacent BSS data\",\"size\":\"8 bytes per pointer slot\"},\"impact\":[{\"type\":\"OOB_READ\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[rand_idx]) at 0x156e dereferences an OOB pointer from msg[] as a string, potentially leaking memory contents or crashing.\"},{\"type\":\"OOB_WRITE\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"msg[rand_idx] = msg[cookie_num-1] at 0x15c6 and msg_size[rand_idx] = msg_size[cookie_num-1] at 0x15fc write to OOB locations in BSS, potentially corrupting msg_size[], urandom, or cookie_num.\"},{\"type\":\"MEMORY_CORRUPTION\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"free(msg[rand_idx]) at 0x158e frees an OOB pointer value from msg[], which could be a non-heap pointer (e.g., a FILE* or integer value), causing heap corruption or crash.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E008\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1530-0x1533\",\"description\":\"mov eax,DWORD PTR [rbp-0xc] loads the 1-byte fread result as a 32-bit int. cdqe sign-extends eax to rax. If the byte >= 0x80, rax becomes negative (e.g., 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFF80).\"},{\"id\":\"E009\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x153c-0x153e\",\"description\":\"cqo sign-extends rax to rdx:rax, then idiv rcx performs signed division by cookie_num. The remainder in rdx can be negative (range -(cookie_num-1) to cookie_num-1).\"},{\"id\":\"E010\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x154a-0x154c\",\"description\":\"cdqe sign-extends the 32-bit rand_idx to 64-bit again, then lea rdx,[rax*8+0x0] uses it as an unsigned offset multiplier. A negative rax produces a negative offset from msg base (0x4060).\"},{\"id\":\"E011\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x156e\",\"description\":\"printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[rand_idx]) — dereferences the OOB-retrieved value as a string pointer\"},{\"id\":\"E012\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x158e\",\"description\":\"free(msg[rand_idx]) — frees the OOB-retrieved pointer value, which may not be a valid heap pointer\"},{\"id\":\"E013\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x15c6\",\"description\":\"mov QWORD PTR [rcx+rdx*1],rax — writes msg[cookie_num-1] value to OOB location msg[rand_idx], corrupting BSS data\"}],\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"verification_required\":[\"Confirm at runtime that a urandom byte with MSB set produces a negative rand_idx\",\"Verify the probability: approximately 50% of random bytes have MSB set, so the negative index occurs frequently\",\"Confirm the OOB free and OOB write cause observable corruption\"]},{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-003\",\"title\":\"STALE_POINTER_AFTER_FREE_IN_EAT_COOKIE\",\"root_cause\":{\"type\":\"Use-After-Free\",\"description\":\"In eat_cookie, after free(msg[rand_idx]), the code copies msg[cookie_num-1] to msg[rand_idx] and msg_size[cookie_num-1] to msg_size[rand_idx], then decrements cookie_num. However, the old slot msg[cookie_num-1] is NOT cleared (set to NULL) after the copy. The freed pointer (which was at msg[rand_idx] and has been overwritten) is no longer directly accessible, but if rand_idx == cookie_num-1 (the random index equals the last valid index), the copy is a self-assignment (msg[cookie_num-1] = msg[cookie_num-1]) and the freed pointer remains in the slot. After cookie_num--, this slot is at index cookie_num (new value), which is 'out of active range' but still in memory. Combined with the OOB index bug (BUG-001), this freed pointer can be accessed via edit_cookie or read_cookie using a large unsigned index that passes the signed check.\"},\"affected_functions\":[\"eat_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\"],\"affected_objects\":[\"msg[] array at 0x4060\",\"msg_size[] array at 0x4160\",\"cookie_num at 0x41e8\"],\"attack_surface\":{\"input\":\"random_byte from /dev/urandom (determines rand_idx) + OOB index via scanf in edit/read_cookie\",\"entry_function\":\"eat_cookie (trigger) + edit_cookie/read_cookie (exploit)\",\"data_flow\":[\"eat_cookie: free(msg[rand_idx]) at 0x158e — pointer freed\",\"eat_cookie: msg[rand_idx] = msg[cookie_num-1] at 0x15c6 — if rand_idx == cookie_num-1, self-assignment, freed pointer stays\",\"eat_cookie: cookie_num-- at 0x160a — slot now at index cookie_num (out of active range)\",\"edit_cookie/read_cookie: OOB index (BUG-001) reaches the stale slot at old cookie_num-1 position\",\"edit_cookie: read(0, msg[stale_slot], msg_size[stale_slot]-1) — writes to freed memory\",\"read_cookie: printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[stale_slot]) — reads from freed memory\"]},\"security_check\":{\"expected\":\"After moving msg[cookie_num-1] to msg[rand_idx], the source slot msg[cookie_num-1] should be set to NULL to prevent stale pointer access\",\"actual\":\"msg[cookie_num-1] is not cleared after the copy; the freed/moved pointer remains in the old slot\",\"missing_or_incorrect\":\"Missing NULL assignment to msg[cookie_num-1] after the move operation\"},\"vulnerable_operation\":{\"operation\":\"Dereference of freed heap pointer via msg[] array slot that was not cleared\",\"address\":\"0x15c6 (missing clear), 0x16d2/0x17ce (dereference via OOB index)\",\"expression\":\"msg[old_cookie_num-1] still holds freed pointer after eat_cookie; accessible via OOB index in edit/read_cookie\",\"target\":\"freed heap chunk\",\"size\":\"8 bytes (pointer)\"},\"impact\":[{\"type\":\"OOB_READ\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"read_cookie with an OOB index reaching the stale slot dereferences the freed pointer via printf(\\\"%s\\\"), reading freed heap memory contents.\"},{\"type\":\"OOB_WRITE\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"edit_cookie with an OOB index reaching the stale slot writes to the freed heap chunk via read(0, msg[stale_slot], msg_size[stale_slot]-1), corrupting freed heap memory.\"},{\"type\":\"MEMORY_CORRUPTION\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"Writing to freed heap memory can corrupt heap metadata or overlapping allocations, leading to broader heap corruption.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E014\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x158e\",\"description\":\"free(msg[rand_idx]) — frees the heap pointer at the random index\"},{\"id\":\"E015\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x15b0-0x15c6\",\"description\":\"mov rax,[rcx+rax*1] loads msg[cookie_num-1], then mov [rcx+rdx*1],rax writes it to msg[rand_idx]. If rand_idx == cookie_num-1, this is a self-assignment and the freed pointer remains in the slot.\"},{\"id\":\"E016\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1593-0x160a\",\"description\":\"After the copy, cookie_num is decremented at 0x160a. The old msg[cookie_num-1] slot (now at index cookie_num after decrement) is never set to NULL. No instruction clears this slot.\"},{\"id\":\"E017\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie/read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1681/0x17aa\",\"description\":\"The OOB index bug (BUG-001) in edit_cookie and read_cookie allows accessing msg[] slots beyond the active range (index >= cookie_num). The stale freed pointer at the old cookie_num-1 position (now at index = new cookie_num) can be reached using an OOB index that passes the signed jl check.\"}],\"confidence\":\"MEDIUM\",\"verification_required\":[\"Confirm that rand_idx == cookie_num-1 occurs (probability 1/cookie_num per eat_cookie call)\",\"Verify that the OOB index in edit/read_cookie can reach the stale slot at the old cookie_num-1 position\",\"Confirm the freed pointer is still present in the slot after eat_cookie returns\"]},{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-004\",\"title\":\"NEGATIVE_LENGTH_BYPASS_IN_CREATE_COOKIE\",\"root_cause\":{\"type\":\"Signedness Error\",\"description\":\"In create_cookie, the message length is read via scanf(\\\"%lld\\\") as signed long long, then checked with 'cmp rax,0x100; jle' (signed less-than-or-equal). Negative values (e.g., -1) pass this check since -1 <= 0x100 (signed). The negative length is then passed to calloc(length, 1) where it is implicitly converted to size_t (unsigned), becoming a very large value (e.g., 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF for -1). calloc will fail and return NULL for such large sizes. Subsequently, read(0, NULL, large_value) is called, and the return value is used to index into the NULL buffer, causing a NULL pointer dereference or undefined behavior. Additionally, a length of 0 passes the check, leading to a zero-size allocation that causes a size underflow in edit_cookie (see BUG-005).\"},\"affected_functions\":[\"create_cookie\"],\"affected_objects\":[\"calloc buffer (heap)\",\"msg[cookie_num]\",\"msg_size[cookie_num]\"],\"attack_surface\":{\"input\":\"message_length via scanf(\\\"%lld\\\") from stdin\",\"entry_function\":\"create_cookie\",\"data_flow\":[\"stdin -> scanf(\\\"%lld\\\") -> rbp-0x18 (signed long long length)\",\"cmp rax,0x100; jle at 0x13f6-0x13fc — signed check, negative values pass\",\"calloc(length, 1) at 0x1416 — negative length converted to huge size_t, returns NULL\",\"read(0, NULL, huge_length) at 0x1443 — read with NULL buffer\",\"movsxd rdx,eax at 0x144e — read return value sign-extended\",\"add rax,rdx at 0x1455 — rax is NULL (0), so accesses address = read_return_value\",\"movzx eax,BYTE PTR [rax] at 0x1458 — dereferences potentially invalid address\"]},\"security_check\":{\"expected\":\"Length should be validated as unsigned and within [1, 256] using unsigned comparison\",\"actual\":\"Length is read as signed long long and checked with jle (signed <= 0x100), allowing negative values to pass\",\"missing_or_incorrect\":\"Missing lower bound check (length > 0); signed comparison allows negative values\"},\"vulnerable_operation\":{\"operation\":\"calloc with negative/huge size returning NULL, then dereference via read return value\",\"address\":\"0x1416 (calloc), 0x1443 (read), 0x1458 (dereference)\",\"expression\":\"calloc(negative_length, 1) returns NULL; read(0, NULL, huge); *(NULL + read_return) dereferenced\",\"target\":\"NULL pointer / invalid address\",\"size\":\"1 byte dereference at 0x1458\"},\"impact\":[{\"type\":\"NULL_POINTER_DEREF\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"When length is negative, calloc returns NULL. read(0, NULL, huge) likely returns -1 (EFAULT) or 0. The code then dereferences *(NULL + return_value) at 0x1458, causing a NULL or near-NULL pointer dereference, leading to SIGSEGV.\"},{\"type\":\"CRASH\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"The NULL pointer dereference at 0x1458 causes a segmentation fault, crashing the program.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E018\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x13e1-0x13e8\",\"description\":\"scanf called with format string \\\"%lld\\\" (at 0x2171 in .rodata), reading length as signed long long into rbp-0x18\"},{\"id\":\"E019\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x13f6-0x13fc\",\"description\":\"cmp rax,0x100 followed by jle 0x140a — signed less-than-or-equal comparison. A negative length (e.g., -1) passes since -1 <= 0x100 (signed).\"},{\"id\":\"E020\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1416\",\"description\":\"call calloc@plt — calloc(length, 1) where length is the signed value. calloc's first parameter is size_t (unsigned), so -1 becomes 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, causing allocation failure and NULL return.\"},{\"id\":\"E021\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1443-0x1458\",\"description\":\"read(0, NULL_buf, huge_length) called with NULL buffer. Then movsxd rdx,eax sign-extends read return value, add rax,rdx computes NULL + return_value, and movzx eax,BYTE PTR [rax] dereferences this address.\"}],\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"verification_required\":[\"Confirm calloc returns NULL for negative length values at runtime\",\"Verify the dereference at 0x1458 causes SIGSEGV\",\"Check if length=0 creates a zero-size allocation that leads to BUG-005\"]},{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-005\",\"title\":\"SIZE_UNDERFLOW_IN_EDIT_COOKIE_READ_LENGTH\",\"root_cause\":{\"type\":\"Integer Underflow\",\"description\":\"In edit_cookie, the write length for read() is computed as msg_size[index] - 1. The msg_size entry is a 32-bit int loaded at 0x16b6, then 1 is subtracted at 0x16b9. If msg_size[index] is 0 (which can happen if create_cookie is called with length=0, since msg_size[cookie_num] = length = 0), the subtraction 0 - 1 produces -1 (0xFFFFFFFF as 32-bit int). This is then sign-extended to 64-bit via movsxd at 0x16bc, becoming 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, which is passed as the count argument to read(). This causes read() to attempt writing up to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF bytes to the heap buffer, resulting in a massive heap buffer overflow.\"},\"affected_functions\":[\"edit_cookie\",\"create_cookie\"],\"affected_objects\":[\"msg_size[] at 0x4160\",\"heap buffer at msg[index]\"],\"attack_surface\":{\"input\":\"message_length=0 via create_cookie, then edit_cookie on the zero-size cookie\",\"entry_function\":\"create_cookie (sets msg_size=0) + edit_cookie (triggers underflow)\",\"data_flow\":[\"create_cookie: scanf(\\\"%lld\\\") -> length=0, passes jle check (0 <= 0x100)\",\"create_cookie: calloc(0, 1) returns valid pointer to zero-size allocation\",\"create_cookie: msg_size[cookie_num] = 0 at 0x14a9\",\"edit_cookie: mov eax,DWORD PTR [msg_size[index]] at 0x16b6 — loads 0\",\"edit_cookie: sub eax,0x1 at 0x16b9 — 0 - 1 = 0xFFFFFFFF (32-bit underflow)\",\"edit_cookie: movsxd rdx,eax at 0x16bc — sign-extends to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\",\"edit_cookie: read(0, msg[index], 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF) at 0x16de — heap buffer overflow\"]},\"security_check\":{\"expected\":\"The write length should be validated to be > 0 before use, or msg_size should be checked for 0 before subtracting 1\",\"actual\":\"No check for msg_size[index] == 0 before the subtraction; the underflowed value is used directly as read() count\",\"missing_or_incorrect\":\"Missing validation that msg_size[index] > 0 before computing msg_size[index] - 1\"},\"vulnerable_operation\":{\"operation\":\"read() with underflowed count argument writing to heap buffer\",\"address\":\"0x16b9 (subtraction), 0x16de (read call)\",\"expression\":\"read(0, msg[index], (size_t)(int)(msg_size[index] - 1)) where msg_size[index]=0 produces count=0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\",\"target\":\"heap buffer at msg[index] (zero-size calloc allocation)\",\"size\":\"up to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF bytes (practically: writes until page boundary or crash)\"},\"impact\":[{\"type\":\"OOB_WRITE\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"read() writes attacker-controlled data beyond the zero-size heap buffer, overflowing into adjacent heap chunks and metadata.\"},{\"type\":\"HEAP_BUFFER_OVERFLOW\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"The zero-size calloc allocation provides no writable space, but read() attempts to write a huge amount of data starting at the allocation address, overflowing into adjacent heap memory.\"},{\"type\":\"MEMORY_CORRUPTION\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"The heap overflow corrupts adjacent heap chunks and metadata, potentially leading to broader heap corruption.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E022\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x13f6-0x13fc\",\"description\":\"cmp rax,0x100; jle — length=0 passes the signed check (0 <= 0x100)\"},{\"id\":\"E023\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x14a9\",\"description\":\"mov DWORD PTR [rdx+rax*1],ecx stores length (0) into msg_size[cookie_num]. ecx = edx = lower 32 bits of the signed length value.\"},{\"id\":\"E024\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16b6-0x16b9\",\"description\":\"mov eax,DWORD PTR [rdx+rax*1] loads msg_size[index] (0), then sub eax,0x1 produces 0xFFFFFFFF (32-bit underflow)\"},{\"id\":\"E025\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16bc-0x16de\",\"description\":\"movsxd rdx,eax sign-extends 0xFFFFFFFF to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, then this value is passed as the third argument (count) to read(0, msg[index], count) at 0x16de\"}],\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"verification_required\":[\"Confirm that create_cookie with length=0 stores msg_size=0\",\"Verify that edit_cookie on a zero-size cookie produces read() with count=0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\",\"Confirm the heap overflow occurs before read() returns or crashes\"]}],\"non_vulnerabilities\":[{\"function\":\"main\",\"description\":\"Menu choice read via scanf(\\\"%lld\\\") and dispatched via switch/case (cmp rax,1..5; jne). No memory operations on user input beyond dispatching to handler functions.\",\"reason\":\"The menu choice is only used for control flow dispatch (1-5), not for memory access or pointer arithmetic. No vulnerability in main itself.\"},{\"function\":\"menu\",\"description\":\"Prints menu options via puts(). No user input processing.\",\"reason\":\"Pure output function with no input or memory operations.\"},{\"function\":\"_abort\",\"description\":\"Prints error message via printf and calls exit(1).\",\"reason\":\"No user-controlled input reaches this function's format string; the message is a static string. No vulnerability.\"},{\"function\":\"init\",\"description\":\"Initializes stdio buffers, sets alarm(60), opens /dev/urandom, creates 5 initial cookies via strdup with hardcoded fortune strings.\",\"reason\":\"All inputs are hardcoded strings; no user-controlled data. The urandom NULL check is present. No vulnerability.\"}],\"unresolved\":[{\"description\":\"Whether the eat_cookie signed division negative index (BUG-002) can be triggered reliably and what BSS data it corrupts\",\"reason\":\"The random byte from /dev/urandom is not attacker-controlled, but approximately 50% of bytes have MSB set, making the negative index probabilistically frequent. The exact BSS location accessed depends on the byte value and cookie_num.\",\"required_next_step\":\"Runtime verification: call eat_cookie multiple times and observe whether negative rand_idx causes OOB access, crash, or corruption. Check if the OOB free corrupts heap metadata.\"},{\"description\":\"Whether the UAF stale pointer (BUG-003) can be reliably triggered given the dependency on rand_idx == cookie_num-1\",\"reason\":\"The UAF requires the random index to equal cookie_num-1 (probability 1/cookie_num per call). Combined with the OOB index bug (BUG-001), the stale pointer can be accessed, but the exact sequence needs runtime confirmation.\",\"required_next_step\":\"Runtime verification: call eat_cookie until rand_idx == cookie_num-1, then use edit_cookie/read_cookie with OOB index to access the stale slot. Confirm the freed pointer is still present.\"},{\"description\":\"CET (IBT/SHSTK) status unknown — may affect control-flow exploitation but does not affect memory corruption analysis\",\"reason\":\"checksec did not report CET flags. This is a mitigation concern for S3/S4, not relevant to S2 root cause analysis.\",\"required_next_step\":\"Run readelf -n to check GNU_PROPERTY notes for CET flags.\"},{\"description\":\"ASLR status at runtime not confirmed\",\"reason\":\"Requires runtime observation. PIE is enabled per S1, but ASLR effectiveness depends on kernel configuration.\",\"required_next_step\":\"Runtime observation of address randomization. This is a mitigation concern for S3/S4.\"}]},\"primitive_reports\":[],\"target_bug\":\"\",\"bug_reports\":[],\"impact_reports\":[],\"strategy_reports\":[],\"final_exploit_path\":\"\",\"final_report\":{}}",
  "vulnerability_report": {
    "schema": "VulnerabilityReport",
    "version": "1.0",
    "status": "COMPLETED",
    "summary": {
      "total_bugs": 5,
      "high_severity": 3,
      "medium_severity": 2,
      "low_severity": 0
    },
    "vulnerabilities": [
      {
        "bug_id": "BUG-001",
        "title": "INDEX_SIGNEDNESS_MISMATCH_IN_EDIT_AND_READ_COOKIE",
        "root_cause": {
          "type": "Signedness Error",
          "description": "In edit_cookie and read_cookie, the cookie index is read via scanf(\"%llu\") as unsigned long long, but the bounds check uses 'jl' (signed less-than) to compare index against cookie_num. Any value with bit 63 set (>= 0x8000000000000000) is interpreted as negative by the signed jl comparison and passes the check (since a large negative is < cookie_num). The index is then used as an unsigned multiplier in 'lea rdx,[rax*8]' to address the msg[] array at 0x4060, producing an out-of-bounds access to arbitrary BSS locations relative to msg[]."
        },
        "affected_functions": [
          "edit_cookie",
          "read_cookie"
        ],
        "affected_objects": [
          "msg[32] at 0x4060",
          "msg_size[32] at 0x4160",
          "urandom FILE* at 0x41e0",
          "cookie_num at 0x41e8",
          "stdout at 0x4020",
          "stdin at 0x4030",
          "stderr at 0x4040"
        ],
        "attack_surface": {
          "input": "cookie_index via scanf(\"%llu\") from stdin",
          "entry_function": "edit_cookie / read_cookie",
          "data_flow": [
            "stdin -> scanf(\"%llu\") -> rbp-0x10 (unsigned long long index)",
            "index loaded into rdx at 0x1676/0x179f",
            "cookie_num loaded into rax at 0x167a/0x17a3",
            "cmp rdx,rax; jl (signed comparison) at 0x1681-0x1684 / 0x17aa-0x17ad",
            "index used in lea rdx,[rax*8] for msg[] addressing at 0x16c3/0x17bf",
            "edit_cookie: read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1) — OOB write",
            "read_cookie: printf(\"%s\", msg[index]) — OOB read + dereference"
          ]
        },
        "security_check": {
          "expected": "Index should be validated as unsigned (0 <= index < cookie_num) using unsigned comparison (jb/jae)",
          "actual": "Index is compared with 'jl' (signed less-than), which treats values >= 0x8000000000000000 as negative and allows them to pass the check",
          "missing_or_incorrect": "Missing unsigned bounds check; signed comparison jl used instead of unsigned jb for an unsigned input"
        },
        "vulnerable_operation": {
          "operation": "OOB array access via lea rdx,[rax*8] + msg base",
          "address": "0x16c3 (edit_cookie), 0x17bf (read_cookie)",
          "expression": "msg[index] where index is attacker-controlled unsigned value that bypassed signed check",
          "target": "msg[] array at 0x4060 and adjacent BSS data (msg_size at 0x4160, urandom at 0x41e0, cookie_num at 0x41e8, stdout/stdin/stderr at 0x4020-0x4040)",
          "size": "8 bytes per pointer slot for msg[], 4 bytes per int slot for msg_size[]"
        },
        "impact": [
          {
            "type": "OOB_WRITE",
            "status": "CANDIDATE",
            "reason": "In edit_cookie, the OOB index is used to compute msg[index] address and msg_size[index] value. read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1) writes attacker-controlled data to the OOB-retrieved pointer location. If the OOB slot contains a pointer to a sensitive BSS location (e.g., urandom FILE*, cookie_num), the write corrupts that data."
          },
          {
            "type": "OOB_READ",
            "status": "CANDIDATE",
            "reason": "In read_cookie, the OOB index retrieves a value from msg[] at an out-of-bounds offset. This value is passed to printf(\"%s\") as a string pointer and dereferenced, leaking memory contents at the address stored in the OOB slot. In edit_cookie, msg_size[index] is read OOB to determine the write length."
          },
          {
            "type": "MEMORY_CORRUPTION",
            "status": "CANDIDATE",
            "reason": "The OOB write in edit_cookie can corrupt BSS data structures including msg_size[], urandom FILE*, and cookie_num, leading to broader memory corruption."
          }
        ],
        "evidence": [
          {
            "id": "E001",
            "type": "STATIC",
            "function": "edit_cookie",
            "address": "0x1665-0x166c",
            "description": "scanf called with format string \"%llu\" (at 0x21c4 in .rodata), reading index as unsigned long long into rbp-0x10"
          },
          {
            "id": "E002",
            "type": "STATIC",
            "function": "edit_cookie",
            "address": "0x1681-0x1684",
            "description": "cmp rdx,rax followed by jl 0x1692 — signed less-than comparison. rdx holds the unsigned index, rax holds cookie_num. A value like 0xfffffffffffffff8 (-8 signed) passes this check since -8 < 5 (signed)."
          },
          {
            "id": "E003",
            "type": "STATIC",
            "function": "edit_cookie",
            "address": "0x16c3-0x16d2",
            "description": "lea rcx,[rax*8+0x0] then lea rax,[rip+0x298e] (# 4060 <msg>); mov rax,[rcx+rax*1] — index used as unsigned multiplier to address msg[] array. With index=0xfffffffffffffff8, computes 0x4060 + (-8*8) = 0x4060 - 0x40 = 0x4020 (stdout)."
          },
          {
            "id": "E004",
            "type": "STATIC",
            "function": "read_cookie",
            "address": "0x178e-0x1795",
            "description": "scanf called with format string \"%llu\" (at 0x21c4), reading index as unsigned long long into rbp-0x10"
          },
          {
            "id": "E005",
            "type": "STATIC",
            "function": "read_cookie",
            "address": "0x17aa-0x17ad",
            "description": "cmp rdx,rax followed by jl 0x17bb — same signed less-than comparison as edit_cookie, same bypass"
          },
          {
            "id": "E006",
            "type": "STATIC",
            "function": "read_cookie",
            "address": "0x17bf-0x17ce",
            "description": "lea rdx,[rax*8+0x0] then lea rax,[rip+0x2892] (# 4060 <msg>); mov rax,[rdx+rax*1] — OOB index used to load pointer from msg[], then passed to printf as %s argument at 0x17e1"
          },
          {
            "id": "E007",
            "type": "DERIVED",
            "function": "edit_cookie/read_cookie",
            "address": "0x4060",
            "description": "BSS layout analysis: msg[0] at 0x4060, msg[31] at 0x4158. Negative index -8 (0xfffffffffffffff8) addresses 0x4060-0x40=0x4020 (stdout). Positive OOB: index 32 addresses 0x4160 (msg_size[0]), index 64 addresses 0x41e0 (urandom), index 65 addresses 0x41e8 (cookie_num)."
          }
        ],
        "confidence": "HIGH",
        "verification_required": [
          "Confirm that scanf(\"%llu\") with input like 18446744073709551608 (0xfffffffffffffff8) passes the jl check at runtime",
          "Verify the OOB write in edit_cookie can reach msg_size[], urandom, or cookie_num fields",
          "Verify the OOB read in read_cookie leaks memory via printf(\"%s\") dereferencing an OOB pointer value"
        ]
      },
      {
        "bug_id": "BUG-002",
        "title": "SIGNED_DIVISION_NEGATIVE_INDEX_IN_EAT_COOKIE",
        "root_cause": {
          "type": "Signedness Error",
          "description": "In eat_cookie, a random byte from /dev/urandom is loaded as a 32-bit int, sign-extended to 64-bit via cdqe, then divided by cookie_num using idiv (signed division). If the random byte has its MSB set (>= 0x80), the sign-extended value is negative, and the signed division produces a negative remainder. This negative rand_idx is then sign-extended again via cdqe and used as an unsigned multiplier in 'lea rdx,[rax*8]' to index the msg[] array, producing an out-of-bounds access."
        },
        "affected_functions": [
          "eat_cookie"
        ],
        "affected_objects": [
          "msg[32] at 0x4060",
          "msg_size[32] at 0x4160"
        ],
        "attack_surface": {
          "input": "random_byte from /dev/urandom (fread 1 byte)",
          "entry_function": "eat_cookie",
          "data_flow": [
            "/dev/urandom -> fread -> rbp-0xc (1 byte stored as int)",
            "mov eax,[rbp-0xc] at 0x1530 — loads byte as 32-bit int",
            "cdqe at 0x1533 — sign-extends to 64-bit (negative if MSB set)",
            "cqo at 0x153c — sign-extends for division",
            "idiv rcx at 0x153e — signed division by cookie_num, remainder in rdx",
            "rand_idx = remainder stored at rbp-0xc at 0x1544",
            "cdqe at 0x154a — sign-extends rand_idx again",
            "lea rdx,[rax*8] at 0x154c — used as unsigned offset to index msg[]",
            "printf(\"%s\", msg[rand_idx]) at 0x156e — OOB read + dereference",
            "free(msg[rand_idx]) at 0x158e — OOB free",
            "msg[rand_idx] = msg[cookie_num-1] at 0x15c6 — OOB write",
            "msg_size[rand_idx] = msg_size[cookie_num-1] at 0x15fc — OOB write"
          ]
        },
        "security_check": {
          "expected": "Random index should be computed as unsigned modulo: (unsigned char)byte % cookie_num, producing range [0, cookie_num-1]",
          "actual": "Byte is loaded as signed int, sign-extended, and divided with idiv (signed), producing a remainder in range [-(cookie_num-1), cookie_num-1]",
          "missing_or_incorrect": "Missing unsigned conversion of the random byte before division; signed idiv used instead of unsigned div"
        },
        "vulnerable_operation": {
          "operation": "OOB array access via lea rdx,[rax*8] + msg base, used for printf, free, and pointer assignment",
          "address": "0x154c-0x15c6",
          "expression": "msg[rand_idx] where rand_idx = (signed int)random_byte % cookie_num (signed idiv), can be negative",
          "target": "msg[] array at 0x4060 and adjacent BSS data",
          "size": "8 bytes per pointer slot"
        },
        "impact": [
          {
            "type": "OOB_READ",
            "status": "CANDIDATE",
            "reason": "printf(\"%s\", msg[rand_idx]) at 0x156e dereferences an OOB pointer from msg[] as a string, potentially leaking memory contents or crashing."
          },
          {
            "type": "OOB_WRITE",
            "status": "CANDIDATE",
            "reason": "msg[rand_idx] = msg[cookie_num-1] at 0x15c6 and msg_size[rand_idx] = msg_size[cookie_num-1] at 0x15fc write to OOB locations in BSS, potentially corrupting msg_size[], urandom, or cookie_num."
          },
          {
            "type": "MEMORY_CORRUPTION",
            "status": "CANDIDATE",
            "reason": "free(msg[rand_idx]) at 0x158e frees an OOB pointer value from msg[], which could be a non-heap pointer (e.g., a FILE* or integer value), causing heap corruption or crash."
          }
        ],
        "evidence": [
          {
            "id": "E008",
            "type": "STATIC",
            "function": "eat_cookie",
            "address": "0x1530-0x1533",
            "description": "mov eax,DWORD PTR [rbp-0xc] loads the 1-byte fread result as a 32-bit int. cdqe sign-extends eax to rax. If the byte >= 0x80, rax becomes negative (e.g., 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFF80)."
          },
          {
            "id": "E009",
            "type": "STATIC",
            "function": "eat_cookie",
            "address": "0x153c-0x153e",
            "description": "cqo sign-extends rax to rdx:rax, then idiv rcx performs signed division by cookie_num. The remainder in rdx can be negative (range -(cookie_num-1) to cookie_num-1)."
          },
          {
            "id": "E010",
            "type": "STATIC",
            "function": "eat_cookie",
            "address": "0x154a-0x154c",
            "description": "cdqe sign-extends the 32-bit rand_idx to 64-bit again, then lea rdx,[rax*8+0x0] uses it as an unsigned offset multiplier. A negative rax produces a negative offset from msg base (0x4060)."
          },
          {
            "id": "E011",
